Basic Blueprint Reading — Costin and Linn-Benton (@ql-source-blueprint: 0, is #book, #part-of @ql-sources) { r_3BSMCZ60NQ4ESQ5YK6K2JAB7F5
Ric Costin, with Linn-Benton Community College's engineering, drafting, and welding teaching material. Basic Blueprint Reading. Open Oregon Educational Resources, 2019. English. Ebook ISBN 978-1-63635-031-8.

[Publisher's book](https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/blueprint/) · [Contents](https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/blueprint/table-of-contents/) · [Introduction and licence](https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/blueprint/front-matter/introduction/).

Read the instructional units completely: The Language of Lines, Visualization, Technical Sketching, Scaling, Dimensioning, Auxiliary Views, Sectional Views, Machined Features, and Print Interpretation. A small object and a paper sketch are enough for the first exercises. Practice interpreting a drawing before relying on a CAD application's attractive image.

The book states CC BY 4.0, copyright Linn-Benton Community College, except where separately noted. Credit Costin, the college, title, and source and preserve individual credits. Its conventions provide a teaching introduction; an actual design needs the drawing's stated projection, units, tolerancing convention, and applicable specification.

Publisher metadata, contents, and accessible sample units checked on 28 October 2026. The host intermittently returns access errors to automated readers; the contents and official indexed metadata were available. Do not describe the entire book as locally inspected or retained. No copy is bundled.

**Return:** [Quantitative literacy sources — books, standards, and articles](../Sources.lingua#r_7MMXWNA1B4YGA271KMHPPJEK9Q).
